Item 2: recovery can strand a growth request (Marcelo; Chris reproduced it)

Status note: this fix was already squashed locally (before the handshake rule arrived) into
5ea7b0daa447 "drm/asahi: g15: m3: back the PB in 16 MiB chunks after the reply, with a reserve"
on t6031/stack-on-177-review. It is NOT pushed to origin. item2.diff is the tree diff
61d68d9f8bd7 (item 1 head) -> dff6cb9e28a6 (local head), i.e. exactly the fixup. If CHANGES,
I rewrite it; if APPROVED, I apply the message rewording below, push, and log.

FINDING
refill_backing() (g15/pools.rs) returns early whenever recovery.reinit is set. A fragment kill
(recovery.rs retire_outcome) sets reinit while the later same-VM flights are only marked
doomed and can still run and ask for growth. When their reserve is used up, accept() returns
Wait and nothing refills: the request strands until the deadline (and a failed recovery there
fail-stops).

VALIDATION OF THE FINDING: real.
Chris's reproducer, added as harness case pending_reinit_with_a_live_render_refills (one live
render, posted = backed, reinit = true, one request, four passes, assert the queue drained).
Against the old guard (`if self.recovery.reinit {`, run as harness mutation
refill-skip-with-live-render, which restores exactly the old line):
  FAILED pending_reinit_with_a_live_render_refills:
  "growth request stranded: posted=256 backed=256 waits=4 refills=0"
(the same numbers Chris posted). Output on the M3: ~/Projects/build-out/kernel-stack177/i2/old/.

FIX (pools.rs refill_backing)
-        // A pending re-initialization is about to drop the posted count: nothing to back for.
-        if self.recovery.reinit {
+        // A pending re-initialization is about to drop the posted count: nothing to back for,
+        // unless a render published before it still runs (the flights behind a fragment kill
+        // keep asking for growth until they retire).
+        let render = (0..self.engine.flights.len()).any(|i| self.receipts(i).renders != 0);
+        if self.recovery.reinit && !render {
             return;
         }

Deviation from the review's wording ("reinit pending AND no flights live"), deliberately:
the skip is lifted only for a live RENDER flight, not for any flight. Reason: after a level-2
reclaim the posted count stays high until the next render's InitBM while the backing is cut
to keep_chunks(); a compute-only flight published in that window (publish() allows it) would,
with "any flight", make refill_due() true every pass and re-back everything the reclaim just
freed. A compute flight cannot ask for growth (answer_request requires a live render), so it
needs no refill. A render flight cannot be published while reinit is pending without clearing
it (its publication does the InitBM and clears reinit), so a live render with reinit pending
is always one published before the re-init was set: the kill case.

Tests (tools/asahi/g15-pb-growth-tests.py):
- pending_reinit_backs_nothing (had a live flight, required the stalling behaviour) is split:
  - pending_reinit_without_flights_backs_nothing: no flights, posted at the reserve line,
    reinit -> nothing backed; reinit cleared -> one refill;
  - pending_reinit_with_compute_only_backs_nothing: one compute-only flight, posted = backed,
    reinit, 4 passes -> nothing backed;
  - pending_reinit_with_a_live_render_refills: Chris's reproducer; expects
    (waits, refills, requests) = (1, 2, 1), the queue empty, and every record/producer only
    after the running VM mapped its chunk (assert_posted_backed).
- mutations: refill-during-reinit re-anchored (removes the guard -> fails
  ..._without_flights_backs_nothing); new refill-skip-with-live-render (old guard -> fails
  ..._live_render_refills, "growth request stranded"); new refill-for-any-flight
  (`reinit && flights.is_empty()` -> fails ..._compute_only_backs_nothing, "backed for a
  compute-only flight").
- docstring line updated.

